      "side": 1,
      "message": "The only concern I have with pushing updates about the program list only for the current user is the situation below:\n\n1) We use the Radio app as the User A\n2) We switch the current user to User B\n3) The new `programListChunk` is pushed for User B only\n4) We switch the current user to User A back\n5) There is a missing `programListChunk` for User A\n\nSo the User A would have the stale data as the result. I believe the difference between the `fanoutAidlCallbackLocked` function and `onProgramListUpdated` is that the latter receives chunks and is stateful.\n\nTherefore, I would recommend only catching the `DeadObjectException` to prevent the  bug where the user switch is delayed because of dead TunerSessions. Let me know if it makes sense.",
